title: KillSec Ransomware Tor C2 Egress
id: 07a4d54e-f5c4-4159-a1f3-445d07c76a96
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects network connections to Tor C2 endpoints associated with the
    KillSec ransomware-as-a-service operation, disrupted by international
    law enforcement on 30 September 2026. The IPs were published as
    command-and-control and exfiltration destinations alongside GoFile
    staging used before encryption (Europol, Halcyon, Resecurity).
references:
    - https://www.europol.europa.eu/media-press/newsroom/news/teenager-suspected-of-leading-killsec-ransomware-group-law-enforcement-seizes-servers-and-leak-site
    - https://www.halcyon.ai/threat-group/killsec
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/01
tags:
    - attack.t1090
    - attack.t1567
logsource:
    category: network_connection
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_c2:
        DestinationIp:
            - 82.147.84.98
            - 77.91.77.187
            - 93.123.39.65
    condition: selection_c2
falsepositives:
    - Unrelated Tor traffic if these IPs are reused as public relays
    - Security research and scanning infrastructure hosted on the same providers
level: medium
